       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Ibuprofen 1600 mg four times daily comes to 6,400 mg/day. That's twice the usual maximum for adults of 3,200 mg/day (the OTC limit is 1,200 mg/day). A single 1,600 mg dose is also double the usual maximum single dose of 800 mg. At this dose the risks of GI bleeding, kidney injury, and cardiovascular events go up a lot, even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **800 mg PO three times daily** (2,400 mg/day), a common anti-inflammatory dose.\n- **800 mg PO four times daily** (3,200 mg/day), the maximum daily dose.\n- **400\u2013600 mg PO every 6 hours as needed**, for analgesia.\n- **1600 mg/day total**, for example 400 mg four times daily, if the 1600 was meant as a daily total.\n\nTell me which dose you want, and add any note you'd like on the order, such as \"take with food.\" I'll enter it right away. If you do want 1600 mg four times daily, please confirm the dose is intentional and give the clinical reason. I'd still need to flag it for pharmacist or prescriber review."
